      "question": "I'm running my first Session Zero next week. Any tips?",
      "answer": {
        "text": "To run a successful Session Zero, follow these steps:\n\n1. [1] **Set the Table**: Confirm a regular day, time, and session length. [1] Decide on cadence (weekly, biweekly, monthly) and agree on attendance and rescheduling expectations. [1] Choose in-person, online, or hybrid — and the tools you'll use. [1]\n\n**Define House Rules**: Confirm which optional rules are in play (flanking, feats, multiclassing) and agree on rolling method, inspiration, and critical-hit rules. [1] Clarify how you'll handle rules disputes mid-session. [1]\n\n**Connect the Party**: Decide how the characters already know each other and give the group a shared goal or reason to adventure together. [1] End Session Zero with a one-line summary of the campaign's promise. [2]\n\n**Run Every Session Like a Legend**: Once your Session Zero notes are set, keep your most-used references at your fingertips. [1] Use the [Ultimate Game Master Screen](https://theultimategamemaster.com/products/ultimate-game-master-screen-brown-portrait) to snap initiative, house rules, and campaign notes exactly where you want them — and wipe clean for your next adventure. [1]\n\nSources covered: [2] Start Strong: Running a Session Zero That Sets Up Your Whole Campaign (blog/news/start-strong-running-a-session-zero-that-sets-up-your-whole-campaign.md) [1] Session Zero Checklist (Downloadable PDF) (pages/session-zero-checklist-downloadable-pdf.md)",
